sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: simple task VM slots (2026-11-05 redesign). A slot is a normal task VM, enrolled ahead of time by today's tasks:provision and kept stopped. Claim = start a ready one. Release = destroy it. The pool refills by enrolling a new one. No snapshots, no identity volume, no baked slot units, no new state machine.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · task VM slots (enrol, claim, release, refill)
  %% kind: task_vm.slots
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Slot VM<br/>normal task VM
  Note over GW,VM: Enrol (5 ready per host)
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06):
  %%> - a host keeps slots only when its task VM settings name them: `task_vms.slots` = `{count, project_id, size}`, for example `{"count": 5, "project_id": 46, "size": "large"}`; without it the host has no pool and every provision clones, as today
  %%> - a slot serves one Project and one size, because the claim only fetches: the slot already holds that Project's checkout with its setup done
  %%> - a slot is a task VM row with no group and `slot_project_id` set; while it is stopped and unclaimed it takes no capacity (`max_vms`), because a stopped VM holds disk, not memory; an enrolling slot runs, so it takes capacity
  %%> - one refill rule, run after every enrol, claim, destroy, image promotion and settings change: when no slot of the host is enrolling or being replaced, enrol one if the pool is below `count`, else replace one stale slot
  %%> - a failed enrol keeps its VM for diagnosis and stops the refill of that host until that VM is destroyed
  GW->>SW: Enrol a slot<br/>today's tasks:provision, no task
  %%> Exactly today's path: clone the current task image, boot, enrol (keys, WireGuard, observer), model key, Pi. Runs in the background whenever the pool is below 5.
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06):
  %%> - kind `task_vm.slot_enrol`, workflow `operation-task-vm-slot-enrol`: the VM child of tasks:provision, then its workspace child at the newest green commit of the Project's default branch (bundle clone and the Project setup steps), then "Converge once" (task VM role phases with the NFS export of the checkout)
  %%> - no nested fleet, Route or Processes: the claim starts them for the task
  %%> - the Gateway records on the slot its image and the digest of what the image carries (playbooks, pins, lock files)
  SW->>H: Stop the VM<br/>incus stop
  %%> A stopped VM costs disk, not memory. The Gateway records it as a ready slot.
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review: the row becomes `parked` with no group, the state a parked task VM has today; the host sweep leaves slot rows alone.
  Note over GW,VM: Claim (a task starts)
  GW->>SW: Claim a ready slot<br/>task intent
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06):
  %%> - `tasks:provision` admission takes the oldest ready slot whose Project and size are the group's and whose image and digest are current, on a host with capacity for it; the VM joins the group in the admission transaction
  %%> - no ready slot: the same admission clones a new VM, exactly as today ("ready slot, else clone" of stage 2)
  %%> - the run is today's `operation-task-provision`: it starts the slot instead of creating a VM, fetches instead of cloning, and skips "Converge once", because the slot converged at enrol with the current playbooks and pins
  SW->>H: Start the VM<br/>incus start
  %%> Seconds: the VM is already enrolled.
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review: the start, agent wait and Pi check of today's resume (`task_vm.resume`), as a child of the claim.
  SW->>VM: Fetch the task branch<br/>git fetch · task token
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06):
  %%> - today's workspace child with one change: the bundle that Node 209 cloned with the task token is fetched into the existing checkout (`git fetch`), not cloned, then `git switch -C task-<group> <commit>`
  %%> - the Project setup steps then run again on the warm checkout, so a changed lock file still installs
  SW->>VM: Reset the nested topology<br/>from the seed's ready copies
  %%> Only for tasks that need the topology.
  SW-->>GW: Slot claimed<br/>terminal event
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review: today's provision projection; the claimed VM is `ready` and belongs to the group, and the Gateway runs the refill rule.
  Note over GW,VM: Release (the task ends)
  GW->>SW: Destroy the VM<br/>today's task VM destroy
  %%> Exactly today's destroy. The Gateway then enrols a new slot to refill the pool.
  Note over GW,VM: After a release of Orbit
  GW->>SW: Replace ready slots<br/>enrol from the new task image
  %%> Ready slots made from the old image are destroyed and enrolled again, one at a time, so a slot is always ready.
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review: a slot is stale when its image is not the host's last promoted image or its digest is not the current release's; the refill rule destroys one stale slot with today's destroy, and the end of that destroy enrols its replacement.
